 34MG    1H(34MG,34MG'G):XUNDL-2       2006EL03                           200605
 34MG c  Beam={+34}Mg, target=liquid hydrogen                                   
 34MG c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2006El03:                          
 34MG2c  Phys Rev C 73, 044314 (2006)                                           
 34MG c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), April 27, 2006                        
 34MG c  {+34}Mg particles produced by fragmentation of {+40}Ar beam            
 34MG2c  at 94 MeV/nucleon hitting a {+181}Ta target. The fragments             
 34MG3c  were separated by RIPS fragment separator. The secondary beam          
 34MG4c  of {+34}Mg at 50 MeV/nucleon hit a liquid hydrogen target.             
 34MG5c  The reaction products and scattered particles were detected            
 34MG6c  and identified by a parallel-plate avalanche counter (PPAC) and        
 34MG7c  a silicon detector telescope. Time-of-flight method used for           
 34MG8c  for atomic charge selection. The |g rays measured with an array of     
 34MG9c  146 NaI(Tl) detectors surrounding the target. Deduced mass             
 34MGAc  deformation and neutron deformation parameters.                        
 34MG  L  0            0+                                                       
 34MG  L  685          2+                                                       
 34MG cL $ |b{-mass}=0.68 {I16}, |b{-n}=0.70 {I13}                              
 34MG  G  685      16                                                           
